# Piper TTS behind a Wyoming server. CPU, on every architecture.
#
# THIS USED TO BE A CUDA IMAGE, AND THE MEASUREMENT IS WHY IT IS NOT.
#
# It was built on nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-cudnn-runtime-ubuntu22.04, installing
# piper-tts and wyoming-piper and then swapping the CPU onnxruntime for
# onnxruntime-gpu, purely so that `--use-cuda` was available to A/B against the
# Kokoro services. That A/B has since been run and CUDA LOST:
#
#     --use-cuda measured 2.5x SLOWER
#       - scripts/run-oww-training.sh, and docker/Dockerfile.kokoro
#
# train/corpus/piper.py explains the mechanism: wyoming-piper starts a fresh session
# per request, so under --use-cuda every request pays CUDA context setup. Piper's
# VITS models are small enough that the setup dominates the inference.
#
# So the CUDA base was carrying a flag nobody should enable, and on Apple Silicon it
# was actively harmful: nvidia/cuda images are linux/amd64 only, so `docker compose
# up piper` on an M-series Mac ran the ENTIRE microWakeWord corpus stage under qemu
# emulation - silently, since emulation succeeds. A CPU baseline measured that way
# times the emulator.
#
# WHAT REPLACED IT, AND WHY THERE IS NOTHING LEFT TO BUILD. Strip CUDA from the old
# file and what remains is `pip install piper-tts wyoming-piper` on a Debian base,
# plus an entrypoint - which is precisely what rhasspy/wyoming-piper already is, and
# it publishes linux/amd64 and linux/arm64. The old header called the published
# image inadequate because it "cannot use a GPU no matter what flags it is given".
# That is now a description of what we want.
#
# PINNED, not :latest. The onnx2tf drift between the CUDA and CPU trainer images is
# the cautionary tale: a floating dependency makes the artefact a function of WHEN an
# image was built, and the run tag (<commit>-d<audio hash>) records neither the date
# nor the version. Bump this deliberately.
FROM rhasspy/wyoming-piper:2.4.3

# Voices are downloaded on demand into --download-dir and get large once a
# multi-speaker model like libritts_r is pulled - it carries 904 speakers - so this
# wants to be a mounted volume rather than image layers. See docker-compose.yml.
VOLUME ["/data"]
EXPOSE 10200

# INHERITED FROM THE BASE, NOT RESTATED: the entrypoint and the default command.
# docker-compose.yml passes --uri, --data-dir, --download-dir and --voice explicitly,
# so the CMD here would be shadowed anyway - and restating an entrypoint that
# upstream owns is how the two silently diverge on the next base bump.
#
# `--voice` stays required in that compose command even though voices download on
# demand: without it wyoming-piper exits 2 before binding the port. It is only the
# default for requests that do not name a voice, and train/corpus/piper.py always
# names one.
